  "instructions": [
    "Preheat oven to 400°F (200°C).",
    "Cook ground beef in a large skillet over medium-high heat until browned, breaking into small pieces as it cooks.",
    "Add onion, garlic, cumin, chili powder, salt, and pepper to the skillet. Cook until onion is translucent.",
    "Warm white sauce in a microwave-safe bowl for 30-45 seconds.",
    "Fill cannoli shells with the beef mixture and place on a baking sheet.",
    "Bake in the preheated oven for 5-7 minutes, or until shells are crispy.",
    "Place a cannoli shell on each plate and spoon warm white sauce over the top.",
    "Sprinkle with sauerkraut and italian seasoning.",
    "Serve immediately and enjoy!"
